mind your decisions i'm presh tallwalker  the american invitational mathematics  examination or amy for short is a  qualifying test in america for the  international mathematical olympiad  it's a three-hour test with 15 questions  and calculators are not allowed  every answer on the test is an integer  from 0 to 999  of interest is 1984 amy problem 3  but lest you think the problem is  outdated it was also asked in 2019 to 14  year olds in sweden  in triangle abc pick a point p on the  interior  construct lines through p that are  parallel to the sides of abc  now these triangles have areas of 4  9 and 49  what is the area of triangle abc  pause the video if you'd like to give  this problem a try  and when you're ready keep watching to  learn how to solve this problem  [Music]  so there will be many ways to solve this  problem and if you want to share your  solution method in the comments you can  use this labeling of the diagram  i think this is a little bit of an  alphabet soup so i'm going to explain it  visually  because the lines through p are parallel  all triangles are similar to each other  and they're similar to abc  the area of a triangle is proportional  to its side length squared  another way of saying this is that the  square root of the area is proportional  to the side length of the triangle  the ratio of the areas of these three  triangles is 4 to 9 to 49  because these triangles are similar to  each other the ratio of their sides will  be the square root of the areas  this works out to be two to three to  seven  suppose this side length is two times x  because the triangles are similar this  side length will be 3x and this side  length will be 7x  because all sides are parallel we have  parallelograms and these lengths will be  equal to each other  consequently we can calculate that ac  will have a length that's equal to 12x  the ratio of the sides between abc and  this yellow triangle will be 12 to 2  because it's 12x to 2x  this will simplify to be 6 to 1.  consequently the ratio of their areas  will be 6 squared to 1 squared which  works out to be 36 to 1.  and now we can calculate the answer the  area of triangle abc will be 36 times 4  and therefore the answer is 144  thanks for making mind your decisions  one of the best channels on youtube as  always thanks for watching and thanks  for your support  [Music]  you
 

